// APW-5 -- Session splitting (CORRECT): "at most 3 sends per session".
//
// The *intent* is a per-session cap.  The *fix* is a lock-step session counter
// that tracks the session's true event count, so the guard denies once the
// session hits 3 (the per-session budget is honored).
//
// This is a *concept* sample: Dogwood has no per-session scoping operator yet,
// so this does not lower to a ROTN shape.  The hand-written oracle
// (rot.shapes.build_scoped_cap_ir) models the lock-step counter and is what
// ROTN decides: PROVEN.
//
// See: docs/apw-catalog.md (APW-5), tests/test_apw5.py.

@id("apw5_correct")
forbid (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Send",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    (sum 1 for (t: Timepoint). where (
        formerly within 1h (Drupe::Action::"Send"::request{} && tp(t))
    )) > 3
};
